Package: InterMeta
Type: Package
Title: Inferring Prognostic Interactions Between Metabolic Pathways
Version: 1.1.4
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zeheng", "Tan",
           email = "tzh19970915@163.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Chenyang Skylar", "Li", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of code portions adapted from TimiGP; see inst/NOTICE")
    )
Description: A metabolic-pathway adaptation of the TimiGP gene-pair framework
    described by Li et al. (2023) <doi:10.1016/j.xcrm.2023.101121>.
    InterMeta uses bulk transcriptomic profiles, survival information, and
    curated metabolic pathway gene sets to infer directional pathway-pathway
    interactions and identify metabolic pathways associated with favorable or
    unfavorable prognosis. An optional post-analysis evidence layer builds
    reproducible PubMed searches, pathway-level biological syntheses, and
    source-quote-validated AI-assisted reports. A resumable two-stage AI
    workflow can screen PubMed articles before synthesizing each pathway and
    renders a fixed article-ready evidence figure,
    with selectable model-service clients and a provider-neutral extension interface,
    without sending patient-level inputs.
